{"task_id": "Mbpp/88", "solution": "```python\ndef freq_count(input_list):\n    \"\"\"Accepts a Python list and returns a built-in dict mapping elements to integer counts.\n\n    Raises TypeError if input_list is not a list or if an element in the list is unhashable.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(input_list, list):\n        raise TypeError(\"freq_count expects a list\")\n\n    if not input_list:\n        return {}\n\n    frequency_map = {}\n    for element in input_list:\n        try:\n            hash(element)\n        except TypeError:\n            raise TypeError(\"unhashable element encountered: cannot use as dict key\")\n        frequency_map[element] = frequency_map.get(element, 0) + 1\n    return frequency_map\n```"}
