{"task_id": "Mbpp/94", "solution": "def index_minimum(items):\n    \"\"\"\n    Returns the first value of the tuple with the smallest second value from a list of tuples.\n    Raises ValueError if the input list 'items' is empty.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not items:\n        raise ValueError(\"Input list 'items' cannot be empty.\")\n\n    min_second_value = items[0][1]\n    result_first_value = items[0][0]\n\n    for first_value, second_value in items:\n        if second_value < min_second_value:\n            min_second_value = second_value\n            result_first_value = first_value\n\n    return result_first_value"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/96", "solution": "import math\n\ndef divisor(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Return the number of positive divisors of the integer n.\n    Assumes n is a positive integer.\"\"\"\n    count = 0\n    for i in range(1, int(math.sqrt(n)) + 1):\n        if n % i == 0:\n            if i * i == n:\n                count += 1\n            else:\n                count += 2\n    return count"}
